WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:08.333
<v Narrator>Welcome to Play by Ear. This is an experiment in three independent information channels.</v>

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:38.083
<v Narrator>Left and right listeners should each wear one earbud from the same pair. The screen observer does not listen.</v>

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.583
<v Left>Left listener: remember the word MAPLE. You alone should know this.</v>

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:42.750
<v Right>Right listener: remember the word QUARTZ. You alone should know this.</v>

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:09.000
<v Narrator>Screen observer, watch for the secret shown in the chapter image. Do not tell the listeners yet.</v>

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.667
<v Left>My secret codeword is LUNAR. Do not show this to the right listener.</v>

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.667
<v Right>My secret codeword is COPPER. Do not show this to the left listener.</v>

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:44.167
<v Narrator>Now compare your information. Say the left secret, followed by the right secret, followed by the screen digit.</v>

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:15.333
<v Narrator>This chapter includes a QR code within its artwork. Test whether you can see or scan it.</v>

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:48.417
<v Narrator>Listen for pitch and any unusual difference between the channels.</v>

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:25.083
<v Narrator>This is the transcript test. Search for the unusual phrase violet cucumber semaphore.</v>

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:58.167
<v Narrator>The total duration was chosen deliberately. It should appear as four minutes thirty seven seconds.</v>

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:24.500
<v Narrator>The last seconds are deliberately silent. End of test.</v>
